1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,392
My new watch doesn't track steps. It counts down every single word I am ever allowed to speak.

2
00:00:07,692 --> 00:00:15,708
Twelve thousand left. At first, I thought it was a sick tech joke, a clever marketing gimmick gone wrong.

3
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:22,512
Then I argued with my boss and watched three hundred words vanish instantly into thin air.

4
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:29,820
Now I whisper. Every breath feels like a tax I cannot afford to pay to a silent universe.

5
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:38,616
I stopped calling my mom. I stopped singing in the shower. I became a ghost in my own skin.

6
00:00:38,916 --> 00:00:45,372
Until today, when the counter hit zero and the world did not end. It simply paused.

7
00:00:45,672 --> 00:00:52,152
A robotic voice echoed inside my skull, whispering the final sentence I was destined to utter.

8
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:58,644
I realized I never owned my voice. I was just reading lines from a script written before birth.

9
00:00:58,944 --> 00:01:06,792
My lips move now, forced by a relentless clock, finishing the exact paragraph assigned to my soul.

10
00:01:07,092 --> 00:01:11,724
Are you speaking your own thoughts right now, or just reading from your script?
